var e=[{id:1,slug:`skincare-routine-basics`,title:`How to Build a Simple Skincare Routine`,category:`Skin Care`,date:`August 15, 2026`,author:`Dr. Ananya Sharma`,excerpt:`Discover the foundational steps of a solid daily skincare routine that actually works.`,content:`Building a skincare routine doesn't have to be complicated. Start with three basic steps: cleanse, moisturize, and protect. A gentle cleanser removes dirt, a good moisturizer hydrates, and a broad-spectrum SPF protects against UV damage. Introduce new products slowly to see how your skin reacts.`,image:`https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1556228578-0d85b1a4d571?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=600&h=400`},{id:2,slug:`understanding-acne`,title:`5 Things You Should Know About Acne`,category:`Acne`,date:`July 28, 2026`,author:`Dr. Vikram Rao`,excerpt:`Acne is common, but misunderstood. Here are five facts to help you manage breakouts.`,content:`1. Acne isn't just for teens. 2. Diet can play a role, but it's rarely the only cause. 3. Over-washing can make it worse by stripping natural oils. 4. Spot treatments are helpful but consistency is key. 5. Consult a dermatologist if over-the-counter products fail after a few months.`,image:`https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1616394584738-fc6e612e71b9?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=600&h=400`},{id:3,slug:`sun-protection-matters`,title:`Why Sun Protection Matters Every Day`,category:`Sun Protection`,date:`July 10, 2026`,author:`Dr. Priya Menon`,excerpt:`Sunscreen isn't just for the beach. Learn why daily SPF is your best anti-aging defense.`,content:`UV rays penetrate clouds and windows, causing premature aging and increasing the risk of skin cancer. Using a broad-spectrum SPF 30 or higher every day is the most effective way to protect your skin. Remember to reapply every two hours if you are outdoors.`,image:`https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529335764857-3f1164d1cb24?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=600&h=400`},{id:4,slug:`benefits-of-vitamin-c`,title:`The Hidden Benefits of Vitamin C for Your Skin`,category:`Skin Care`,date:`September 5, 2026`,author:`Dr. Neha Gupta`,excerpt:`Vitamin C is more than just an immune booster—it is a powerhouse for glowing skin.`,content:`Vitamin C is a potent antioxidant that neutralizes free radicals, which cause premature aging. When applied topically, it helps brighten the complexion, even out skin tone, and promote collagen production. For best results, use a serum with L-ascorbic acid in the morning under your sunscreen. Keep the bottle away from direct sunlight to prevent oxidation.`,image:`https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1629198688000-71f23e745b6e?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=600&h=400`},{id:5,slug:`treating-rosacea`,title:`Living with Rosacea: Tips and Treatments`,category:`Conditions`,date:`September 12, 2026`,author:`Dr. Kavya Reddy`,excerpt:`Understanding your triggers is the first step to managing rosacea flare-ups effectively.`,content:`Rosacea is a common but poorly understood condition causing redness and visible blood vessels on the face. Managing it starts with identifying triggers like spicy foods, alcohol, extreme temperatures, and stress. A gentle skincare routine using non-irritating products is crucial. In-clinic treatments, such as laser therapy, can dramatically reduce persistent redness.`,image:`https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1596755389378-c31d21fd1273?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=600&h=400`},{id:6,slug:`anti-aging-myths`,title:`Busting Top 3 Anti-Aging Myths`,category:`Aesthetic`,date:`October 1, 2026`,author:`Dr. Vikram Rao`,excerpt:`Stop wasting money on ineffective products. Let us debunk the most common anti-aging myths.`,content:`Myth 1: You only need anti-aging products in your 40s. Fact: Prevention is easier than correction; starting a good routine in your 20s pays off. Myth 2: Expensive creams work like Botox. Fact: While good creams hydrate and plump the skin, they cannot relax the muscles that cause dynamic wrinkles. Myth 3: Drinking water eliminates wrinkles. Fact: Hydration is vital for overall health, but it won't erase deep set lines.`,image:`https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1515377905703-c4788e51af15?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=600&h=400`}];export{e as t};